  "wire_float_text": {
    "_comment": "The exact `doubleValue` text the reference emits, read off the HTTP body (NOT a re-rendering of a parsed float). protojson uses encoding/json's rule \u2014 exponent form iff |v| < 1e-6 or |v| >= 1e21, with the exponent's leading zero stripped \u2014 so it renders 2e-9, not 2e-09 \u2014 the plan's hypothesised divergence at the small end does NOT exist on the wire. serde_json/ryu agrees everywhere on the reachable ladder EXCEPT 2^10..2^13 ns, where ryu picks exponent form and the reference picks plain decimal. Recorded, not filed: same value, same parse (see AGENT.md).",
